  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-09-06T14:51:12.803Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "From all information I've gathered, VRChat seems to be using Windows's inbuilt media player to display videos among other things\nHowever, for cross-platform compatibility through layers like Wine or Proton, this is a total hassle and the last issue which would have to be solved for it to be fully playable on platforms other than Windows, that being Linux and possibly even MacOS or even BSD if you're willing to go that far.\nBecause otherwise, without a good replacement, users will have to install an OS which they don't want to use just to see videos In-Game, or make a (K)VM and pass through their GPU to that VM, which also isn't convenient as that sacrifices CPU performance\n\nusing something different than WMP might also allow new codecs and other technology to be used which weren't a thing yet back when WMP 12 was written",
